import pf.Html
import intl.Date
import intl.Locales
import intl.Plural
import intl.Catalog
import ../../../Demos/IntlDemo
import ../../../Demos/IntlSamples
import ../../../Ui/Code
import ../../../Ui/Heading
import ../../../Ui/Note
import ../../../Generated/Sources
import ../../../Generated/Paths
import ../../../Ui/PageHero
import ../../../Ui/TableWrap
import ../../../Ui/Demo

## The intl package: how to add it, a live demo (a language picker over numbers, money and dates),
## the same calls in each starter locale, how an app picks the reader's locale and hands it to its
## components, the formatting functions, messages and catalogs (the demo's message among them,
## written at build time), a form's errors, the modules, the data, and what works today. Every
## output on the page is written by the package as the site is built; every listing is picked from
## a file that compiles.
meta = {
	title: "Intl",
	description: "Numbers, money, dates, relative times and translated messages with plurals, as each locale writes them, for Roc Solid apps: the same text from the server and in the browser.",
	toc: [
		{ id: "install", label: "Installing it" },
		{ id: "demo", label: "A first look" },
		{ id: "locales", label: "Ten locales" },
		{ id: "locale", label: "The reader's locale" },
		{ id: "language", label: "<Language>" },
		{ id: "formatting", label: "Formatting" },
		{ id: "messages", label: "Messages" },
		{ id: "forms", label: "A form's errors" },
		{ id: "modules", label: "The modules" },
		{ id: "data", label: "Locale data and size" },
		{ id: "status", label: "Status" },
	],
}

view! = |_|
	<>
		<NoHydration>
			<PageHero
				kicker={[<>{"The ecosystem · "}</>, <code>packages/intl</code>]}
				title="Every reader's language, written the same on the server and in the browser"
			>
				Numbers, money, dates, relative times and translated messages with plurals, written as each reader's
				locale writes them. It is plain Roc on no platform: the server renders a page in the reader's
				language, and the browser <a href={"${Paths.components}#tree"}>hydrates</a> the same text. In the
				demo below, pick a language or change <code>n</code>.
			</PageHero>

			<Heading id="install">Installing it</Heading>
			<p>Name the package in your app's header (<code>main.roc</code>):</p>
			<Code source={"app [program] { intl: \"../packages/intl/main.roc\", pf: platform \"…/server/platform/main.roc\" }"} numbers={Bool.False} />
			<p>
				Both halves of the app, and tests, import its modules. One locale's formatting is an
				<code>Intl</code> value:
			</p>
			<Code source={"import intl.Intl\nimport intl.Locales\n\nintl = Intl.new(Locales.pl)\n\nintl.number(12345.5)            # \"12 345,5\"\nintl.currency(1234.5, \"PLN\")    # \"1234,50 zł\"\nintl.date(moment, Long)         # \"21 listopada 2026\"\nintl.relative(-2, Hour)         # \"2 godziny temu\""} numbers={Bool.False} />
			<p>
				The one component, <code>{"<Language>"}</code>, holds the reader's locale as a context and is a
				picker. rocx copies it into your app when it writes the app's code
				(<a href={"${Paths.ecosystem}#use"}>using a package</a>); <code>import intl.Language</code> imports
				the copy.
			</p>

			<Heading id="demo">A first look</Heading>
		</NoHydration>
		<Demo>
			<div data-demo="intl"><IntlDemo /></div>
		</Demo>
		<NoHydration>
			<p>
				<code>Language.store!</code> makes a store: the reader's <code>Intl</code> in a
				<a href={"${Paths.components}#primitives"}>signal</a>, the supported locales, and a catalog of
				messages. <code>{"<LanguageContext value={store}>"}</code> provides it to everything inside as a
				<a href={"${Paths.components}#contexts"}>context</a>; <code>{"<Language />"}</code> is the picker.
				Picking a language rewrites only the holes that call <code>intl!()</code>. Here
				<code>remember!</code> does nothing, so your choice isn't kept; in an app it sends the choice to an
				endpoint that sets a cookie (<a href="#language">below</a>).
			</p>
			<p>
				The demo's catalog is empty: messages work in the browser too, but would add about 13 KB to the
				wasm every page of this site loads. Its message is under <a href="#messages">Messages</a>, written
				as this page was built.
			</p>
			<Code title={Sources.intl_demo_use.file} source={Sources.intl_demo_use.rocx} />
			<details>
				<summary>The whole demo: <code>{Sources.intl_demo.file}</code></summary>
				<Code title={Sources.intl_demo.file} source={Sources.intl_demo.rocx} />
			</details>

			<Heading id="locales">Ten locales</Heading>
			<p>
				English (American and British), German, French, Spanish, Polish, Czech, Russian, Arabic and
				Japanese, each writing the same calls (as this page was built):
			</p>
			<TableWrap>
				<table class="locales">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Locale</th>
							<th><code>number(-1234567.891)</code></th>
							<th><code>percent(0.256, 1)</code></th>
							<th><code>compact(1234567)</code></th>
							<th><code>{"currency(1234.5, \"EUR\")"}</code></th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{...Locales.all.map(
							|data|
								<tr lang={data.tag}>
									<td><code>{data.tag}</code><span class="name">{data.name}</span></td>
									{...IntlSamples.numbers(data).map(|said| <td><bdi>{said}</bdi></td>)}
								</tr>,
						)}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>
			<TableWrap>
				<table class="locales">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Locale</th>
							<th><code>date(moment, Medium)</code></th>
							<th><code>time(moment, Short)</code></th>
							<th><code>relative(-3, Day)</code></th>
							<th><code>relative_day(-1)</code></th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{...Locales.all.map(
							|data|
								<tr lang={data.tag}>
									<td><code>{data.tag}</code><span class="name">{data.name}</span></td>
									{...IntlSamples.dates(data).map(|said| <td><bdi>{said}</bdi></td>)}
								</tr>,
						)}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>
			<Note>
				The moment is 2026-11-21 15:04:05 UTC. The tests check each locale's output against JavaScript's
				<code>Intl</code> (ICU 78, CLDR 48), and each plural rule against <code>Intl.PluralRules</code>,
				number by number.
			</Note>

			<Heading id="locale">The reader's locale</Heading>
			<p>
				An app lists its supported locales, default first. A request gets the locale its
				<code>locale</code> cookie names (the reader's choice), else the one <code>Accept-Language</code>
				asks for, else the default. <code>{"Locale.wanted(request, \"locale\")"}</code> reads both, most
				wanted first; <code>Intl.choose</code> takes the closest supported locale. <code>pl-PL</code> gets
				<code>pl</code>; without plain <code>en</code>, <code>en-US</code> gets <code>en-GB</code>, not
				another language.
			</p>
			<TableWrap>
				<table>
					<thead><tr><th>Accept-Language</th><th>Read in, of en, en-GB, pl and de</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>
						{...["pl-PL,pl;q=0.9,en;q=0.8", "en-GB,en;q=0.8", "en-US", "fr-CH, fr;q=0.9, de;q=0.7", "ja", ""].map(
							|header| <tr><td><code>{if (header == "") "(none)" else header}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.chosen(header)}</code></td></tr>,
						)}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>
			<p>
				Keep the app's locales and words in one module. A GET <a href={Paths.calls}>endpoint</a> answers
				the request's locale, and the root layout reads it. The server renders in that locale and sends the
				answer with the page, so the browser hydrates in the same one.
			</p>
			<Code title={Sources.intl_i18n.file} source={Sources.intl_i18n.rocx} />
			<details>
				<summary>How the closest locale is found: <code>Locale.best</code> and <code>Locale.wanted</code></summary>
				<Code title={Sources.intl_best.file} source={Sources.intl_best.rocx} />
			</details>

			<Heading id="language">{"<Language>"}</Heading>
			<p>
				The root layout makes the store and provides it. <code>{"<html lang dir>"}</code> follow it, so the
				whole page switches direction for Arabic:
			</p>
			<Code title={Sources.intl_layout.file} source={Sources.intl_layout.rocx} />
			<p>A component reads the context with <code>use_context!</code> and calls <code>intl!()</code> in its holes:</p>
			<Code title={Sources.intl_basket.file} source={Sources.intl_basket.rocx} />
			<p>
				Picking a language switches the page at once, then calls <code>remember!</code>. Here it sends the
				tag to an app endpoint that sets the <code>locale</code> cookie, so the next page is in it too. Its
				<code>post!</code> sets the cookie on an answer of its own, <code>Answer(…)</code>:
			</p>
			<Code title={Sources.intl_endpoint.file} source={Sources.intl_endpoint.rocx} />
			<TableWrap>
				<table>
					<thead><tr><th><code>Language</code></th><th>Is</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><code>Store</code></td><td>what the context holds: <code>{"intl! : () => Intl"}</code>, the reader's; <code>{"choose! : Str => {}"}</code>, to choose another; and <code>supported : List(Locales.Data)</code>, the choices</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>language_context</code></td><td>the context: <code>{"<LanguageContext value={store}>"}</code> provides it, <code>use_context!(Language.language_context)</code> reads it</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"store!({ supported, catalog, tag, remember! })"}</code></td><td>a store in <code>tag</code>'s locale (the closest supported one; a string that isn't a tag gets the default); its <code>choose!(tag)</code> switches it and calls <code>remember!(tag)</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"<Language label={…} />"}</code></td><td>a <code>{"<select>"}</code> of the supported locales, each named in its own language ("English", "polski", "العربية"), the reader's chosen; <code>label</code> names it for screen readers; its class is <code>language</code></td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>
			<Note>
				These four files are from <code>packages/intl/example</code>, a small app that builds on both
				platforms (<code>rocx dev packages/intl/example</code>). It renders in Polish for
				<code>Accept-Language: pl</code>, and in Arabic, right to left, for a <code>locale=ar</code> cookie.
			</Note>
			<details>
				<summary>The component: <code>{Sources.intl_language.file}</code></summary>
				<Code title={Sources.intl_language.file} source={Sources.intl_language.rocx} />
			</details>

			<Heading id="formatting">Formatting</Heading>
			<p>
				<code>Intl.new(Locales.pl)</code> makes an <code>Intl</code> for one locale,
				<code>Intl.choose(supported, wanted)</code> for the closest of several, and
				<code>Intl.for_tag(supported, tag)</code> for a tag (a cookie's). Numbers are <code>Dec</code>, Roc's
				decimal, rounded half away from zero. A moment is milliseconds since the epoch, written in UTC or
				at a fixed offset (<code>intl.in_offset(60)</code> for Central European winter time).
			</p>
			<TableWrap>
				<table>
					<thead><tr><th>Call</th><th>English</th><th>Polish</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><code>number(1234.5)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.number(1234.5)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.number(1234.5)}</code> (from five digits, Polish groups them)</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>number(-1234567.891)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.number(-1234567.891)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.number(-1234567.891)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>fixed(2.5, 2)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.fixed(2.5, 2)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.fixed(2.5, 2)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>int(12345)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.int(12345)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.int(12345)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>percent(0.256, 1)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.percent(0.256, 1)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.percent(0.256, 1)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>compact(1234)</code>, <code>compact(12345678)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.compact(1234)}</code>, <code>{IntlSamples.en.compact(12345678)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.compact(1234)}</code>, <code>{IntlSamples.pl.compact(12345678)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"currency(1234.5, \"EUR\")"}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.currency(1234.5, "EUR")}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.currency(1234.5, "EUR")}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"currency(1234.5, \"PLN\")"}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.currency(1234.5, "PLN")}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.currency(1234.5, "PLN")}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>date(moment, Short)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.date(IntlSamples.moment, Short)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.date(IntlSamples.moment, Short)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>date(moment, Medium)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.date(IntlSamples.moment, Medium)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.date(IntlSamples.moment, Medium)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>date(moment, Long)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.date(IntlSamples.moment, Long)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.date(IntlSamples.moment, Long)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>date(moment, Full)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.date(IntlSamples.moment, Full)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.date(IntlSamples.moment, Full)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>time(moment, Short)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.time(IntlSamples.moment, Short)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.time(IntlSamples.moment, Short)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>date_time(moment, Long, Short)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.date_time(IntlSamples.moment, Long, Short)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.date_time(IntlSamples.moment, Long, Short)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>day(Date.ymd(2026, 1, 5), Long)</code>, a day with no time</td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.day(Date.ymd(2026, 1, 5), Long)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.day(Date.ymd(2026, 1, 5), Long)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>month_year(Date.ymd(2026, 11, 1))</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.month_year(Date.ymd(2026, 11, 1))}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.month_year(Date.ymd(2026, 11, 1))}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>month_name(11)</code>, <code>weekday_name(6)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.month_name(11)}</code>, <code>{IntlSamples.en.weekday_name(6)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.month_name(11)}</code>, <code>{IntlSamples.pl.weekday_name(6)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>relative(-3, Day)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.relative(-3, Day)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.relative(-3, Day)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>relative(2, Hour)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.relative(2, Hour)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.relative(2, Hour)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>relative_day(-1)</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.relative_day(-1)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.relative_day(-1)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>ago(then, now)</code>, five minutes apart</td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.ago(IntlSamples.moment - 300000, IntlSamples.moment)}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.ago(IntlSamples.moment - 300000, IntlSamples.moment)}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>plural(22)</code></td><td><code>{Plural.name(IntlSamples.en.plural(22))}</code></td><td><code>{Plural.name(IntlSamples.pl.plural(22))}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>ordinal(23)</code></td><td><code>{Plural.name(IntlSamples.en.ordinal(23))}</code> ("23rd")</td><td><code>{Plural.name(IntlSamples.pl.ordinal(23))}</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>tag()</code>, <code>name()</code>, <code>direction()</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.en.tag()}</code>, <code>{IntlSamples.en.name()}</code>, <code>{IntlSamples.en.direction()}</code></td><td><code>{IntlSamples.pl.tag()}</code>, <code>{IntlSamples.pl.name()}</code>, <code>{IntlSamples.pl.direction()}</code></td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>
			<p>
				<code>number_with(x, options)</code> takes the fraction digits and grouping
				(<code>{"{ ..NumberFormat.defaults, min_fraction: 2 }"}</code>). <code>ago</code> picks the unit:
				seconds under a minute, then minutes, hours, days (under a week), weeks (under 30 days), months
				(under a year), years. Arabic follows CLDR 48: Latin digits, invisible marks that keep right-to-left
				text in order, and its dual without a digit ("خلال ساعتين", "in two hours").
			</p>

			<Heading id="messages">Messages</Heading>
			<p>
				A catalog holds keyed messages for each locale, one locale the default:
				<code>{"Catalog.new(\"en\", [(\"en\", [(key, message), …]), (\"pl\", […])])"}</code>, as in
				<code>I18n.rocx</code> above. <code>{"intl.t(key, args)"}</code> looks a key up in the reader's
				locale, then its fallbacks (<code>pl-PL</code>, then <code>pl</code>), then the default. So a
				regional set (<code>en-GB</code>) holds only what differs, and a missing translation shows the
				default's words. A key no set has shows as itself, so you spot it.
			</p>
			<p>
				The demo's message, <code>files</code>, in five languages, and what
				<code>{"t(\"files\", [(\"count\", Int(n))])"}</code> says for a few counts. Each language has its own
				plural categories: German two, Polish four (and <code>=0</code>), Arabic six, Japanese one.
			</p>
			<Code title={Sources.intl_files.file} source={Sources.intl_files.rocx} />
			<TableWrap>
				<table class="files">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th><code>n</code></th>
							{...IntlDemo.supported.map(|data| <th><code>{data.tag}</code></th>)}
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{...[0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 11, 22, 100].map(
							|count|
								<tr>
									<td><code>{count.to_str()}</code></td>
									{...IntlDemo.supported.map(|data| <td lang={data.tag}><bdi>{IntlSamples.files(data, count)}</bdi></td>)}
								</tr>,
						)}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>
			<p>
				Messages use a subset of ICU MessageFormat, which translators' tools read and write. Arguments are
				name–value pairs: <code>{"(\"name\", Text(\"Ada\"))"}</code>,
				<code>{"(\"count\", Int(3))"}</code>, <code>{"(\"price\", Num(9.99))"}</code> or
				<code>{"(\"when\", Moment(ms))"}</code>.
			</p>
			<TableWrap>
				<table>
					<thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>With</th><th>Is</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><code>{"Hello, {name}!"}</code></td><td><code>name: Ada</code></td><td>{IntlSamples.say(IntlSamples.en, "Hello, {name}!", [("name", Text("Ada"))])}</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"{count, plural, =0 {No files} one {# file} other {# files}}"}</code></td><td><code>count: 0</code>, <code>1</code>, <code>1234</code></td><td>{Str.join_with([0, 1, 1234].map(|n| IntlSamples.say(IntlSamples.en, "{count, plural, =0 {No files} one {# file} other {# files}}", [("count", Int(n))])), " · ")}</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"{place, selectordinal, one {#st} two {#nd} few {#rd} other {#th}}"}</code></td><td><code>place: 1</code>, <code>22</code>, <code>13</code></td><td>{Str.join_with([1, 22, 13].map(|n| IntlSamples.say(IntlSamples.en, "{place, selectordinal, one {#st} two {#nd} few {#rd} other {#th}}", [("place", Int(n))])), " · ")}</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"{role, select, admin {Administrator} other {Member}}"}</code></td><td><code>role: admin</code>, <code>guest</code></td><td>{Str.join_with(["admin", "guest"].map(|role| IntlSamples.say(IntlSamples.en, "{role, select, admin {Administrator} other {Member}}", [("role", Text(role))])), " · ")}</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"{guests, plural, offset:1 =0 {Nobody} =1 {{host}} one {{host} and # other} other {{host} and # others}}"}</code></td><td><code>host: Ada</code>, <code>guests: 3</code></td><td>{IntlSamples.say(IntlSamples.en, "{guests, plural, offset:1 =0 {Nobody} =1 {{host}} one {{host} and # other} other {{host} and # others}}", [("guests", Int(3)), ("host", Text("Ada"))])}</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"{total, number} · {share, number, percent}"}</code></td><td><code>total: 1234.5</code>, <code>share: 0.25</code></td><td>{IntlSamples.say(IntlSamples.en, "{total, number} · {share, number, percent}", [("total", Num(1234.5)), ("share", Num(0.25))])}</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"{when, date, long} at {when, time, short}"}</code></td><td><code>when: moment</code></td><td>{IntlSamples.say(IntlSamples.en, "{when, date, long} at {when, time, short}", [("when", Moment(IntlSamples.moment))])}</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>{"It''s '{literal}'"}</code></td><td></td><td>{IntlSamples.say(IntlSamples.en, "It''s '{literal}'", [])}</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>
			<p>
				A plural's cases are the locale's plural categories (<code>zero</code>, <code>one</code>,
				<code>two</code>, <code>few</code>, <code>many</code>, <code>other</code>); <code>other</code> is
				required. English has two, Polish four. For
				<code>{"{count, plural, one {# plik} few {# pliki} many {# plików} other {# pliku}}"}</code>:
			</p>
			<TableWrap>
				<table>
					<thead><tr><th>With</th><th>Is</th><th>Because</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>
						{...[("1", "one"), ("3", "few: 2–4, 22–24…"), ("5", "many: the other whole numbers"), ("12", "many: 12–14 too"), ("22", "few"), ("2.5", "other: a fraction")].map(
							|(n, why)| <tr><td><code>count: {n}</code></td><td>{IntlSamples.say(IntlSamples.pl, "{count, plural, one {# plik} few {# pliki} many {# plików} other {# pliku}}", [("count", Text(n))])}</td><td>{why}</td></tr>,
						)}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>
			<p>
				<code>Catalog.problems(catalog)</code> lists what a translator still has to fix: a key missing from a
				locale, a key the default lacks, a message that can't be read (shown as written), and arguments that
				differ from the default's. Add <code>expect Catalog.problems(I18n.catalog) == []</code> to your app's
				tests. For this catalog:
			</p>
			<Code title={Sources.intl_typos.file} source={Sources.intl_typos.rocx} />
			<ul class="problems">
				{...Catalog.problems(IntlSamples.typos).map(|problem| <li>{Catalog.explain(problem)}</li>)}
			</ul>

			<Heading id="forms">A form's errors</Heading>
			<p>
				<a href={Paths.ecosystem_forms}><code>packages/forms</code></a> gives each issue a key and parameters:
				<code>Issues.key(code)</code> is <code>"too_short"</code>, <code>Issues.params(code)</code> is
				<code>{"[{ name: \"min\", value: \"3\" }]"}</code>. <code>intl.issue(key, params)</code> says it in
				the reader's language from <code>Validation.catalog</code>, which words all nineteen of forms' keys
				in every starter locale, in forms' voice ("Use at least 3 characters"). Merge it under the app's
				catalog (<code>Catalog.merge(Validation.catalog, words)</code>), as <code>I18n.rocx</code> does. To
				reword a key, or word one of your own (a <code>Custom</code> issue's), put
				<code>{"validation.<key>"}</code> in the app's catalog (<code>validation.not_postcode</code>).
			</p>
			<TableWrap>
				<table>
					<thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Params</th><th>English</th><th>Polish</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>
						{...[("required", "", ""), ("too_short", "min", "3"), ("too_short", "min", "5"), ("too_large", "max", "1500.5"), ("too_early", "min", "2026-01-31"), ("not_email", "", "")].map(
							|(key, name, value)| {
								params = if (name == "") [] else [{ name, value }]
								<tr>
									<td><code>{key}</code></td>
									<td><code>{if (name == "") "(none)" else "${name}: ${value}"}</code></td>
									<td>{IntlSamples.issue(IntlSamples.en, key, params)}</td>
									<td>{IntlSamples.issue(IntlSamples.pl, key, params)}</td>
								</tr>
							},
						)}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>
			<p>
				A number in the params picks the plural and is written the locale's way; a day
				(<code>too_early</code>, <code>too_late</code>) as the locale writes dates.
			</p>

			<Heading id="modules">The modules</Heading>
			<p>
				Plain Roc, on no platform. <code>roc test packages/intl/main.roc</code> runs their
				<code>expect</code>s. The <a href={"https://github.com/Roc-Solid/rocx/tree/master/packages/intl"}>README</a>
				has every function.
			</p>
			<TableWrap>
				<table>
					<thead><tr><th>Module</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><code>Intl</code></td><td>one locale's way of writing things, and its messages: <code>new</code>, <code>choose</code>, <code>for_tag</code>, <code>with_catalog</code>, <code>in_offset</code>, the functions above, <code>t</code>, <code>format</code> (a message given inline), <code>translated</code>, <code>issue</code>, <code>error</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>Locale</code></td><td>a BCP 47 tag: <code>Locale.parse("EN_us")</code> is <code>en-US</code>; <code>fallbacks</code>; <code>accept_language(header)</code>; <code>best(wanted, supported, default)</code>; <code>wanted(request, cookie)</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>Locales</code></td><td>each starter locale's data: <code>en</code>, <code>en_gb</code>, <code>de</code>, <code>fr</code>, <code>es</code>, <code>pl</code>, <code>cs</code>, <code>ru</code>, <code>ar</code>, <code>ja</code>, and <code>all</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>Plural</code></td><td>CLDR's categories, each language's cardinal and ordinal rules, and <code>Forms</code>, a word for each category</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>NumberFormat</code></td><td>numbers by a locale's <code>Symbols</code>: grouping, fraction digits (<code>Options</code>, <code>defaults</code>), percent, compact, currency</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>Date</code></td><td>a day on the calendar: <code>Date.ymd(2026, 11, 21)</code>, days since 1970, weekdays, adding days and months, <code>parse_iso</code>, <code>to_iso</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>DateFormat</code></td><td>dates and times by CLDR's patterns (<code>d MMMM y</code>), in four styles</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>RelativeTime</code></td><td>"in 3 days", "3 dni temu"; <code>between(ms)</code>, the unit a difference is said in</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>Message</code></td><td>the ICU subset above: <code>parse</code>, <code>format</code>, <code>names</code>, <code>Arg</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>Catalog</code></td><td>messages for each locale: <code>new</code>, <code>empty</code>, <code>add</code>, <code>merge</code>, <code>find</code>, <code>keys</code>, <code>missing</code>, <code>problems</code>, <code>explain</code></td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>Validation</code></td><td>the words for packages/forms' issues, in every starter locale</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</TableWrap>

			<Heading id="data">Locale data and size</Heading>
			<p>
				<code>tools/locales.mjs</code> writes <code>packages/intl/Locales.roc</code> from the CLDR in Node's
				ICU: the symbols, patterns and names for numbers, money, dates and times, and relative-time words
				for each plural category. Plural
				rules are code, in <code>Plural.roc</code>. To add a locale, add it to the script's list (with its
				plural rules if the language is new), run the script, and format the package with
				<code>rocx fmt</code>.
			</p>
			<p>
				An app's wasm holds only the locales it names, under 1 KB (brotli) each. The code is the larger part
				and grows with what the app calls. Measured on 2026-11-21, before the browser's host moved to Rust:
				numbers alone added 12.6 KB to a small app, all the formatting 22.1 KB, and messages too 34.5 KB.
				The demo above added about 17 KB to this site's wasm (the store, the picker, numbers, money, dates
				and relative times in five locales; three would have saved 1.2 KB).
			</p>

			<Heading id="status">Status</Heading>
			<p>
				<strong>Works today</strong>, tested for the ten starter locales: everything above. The example app
				renders on the server, hydrates, switches language in place and keeps the choice in a cookie
				(checked by hand; it has no tests of its own).
			</p>
			<p><strong>Not yet</strong> (each has a proposal in <code>packages/intl/PROPOSALS.md</code>):</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					The app writes the server's side: the endpoint that answers the locale and keeps a choice (as
					above), and any middleware that sends <code>Content-Language</code>.
				</li>
				<li>Message keys are strings, so the compiler doesn't check them. A build step that writes a function for each key from message files would.</li>
				<li>Time is UTC or a fixed offset. Named time zones, which follow summer time, need a host primitive.</li>
				<li>More locales and fuller data (CLDR's parent locales such as <code>en-001</code>, other digits, long compact forms) wait on a generator that reads cldr-json.</li>
			</ul>
		</NoHydration>
	</>

<style>
	/* Code in a table wraps at its spaces, so a long call or message keeps the columns in view; and a
	   heading's code is as it is written, not in capitals. */
	td code,
	th code {
		white-space: normal;
	}

	th code {
		text-transform: none;
		letter-spacing: normal;
	}

	/* Each locale's name for itself, under its tag. */
	.locales .name {
		display: block;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		font-size: var(--size-xs);
		white-space: nowrap;
	}

	.problems {
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}
</style>
